ruling.body:
## Maintainer design ruling: adopt a typed depth and motion grammar

Choose the **typed grammar** direction. The Brutalist family must not normalize every component to one universal `3px` rest shadow and one unconditional lift/sink transition.

Current component-specific P entities are evidence that depth and motion depend on semantic and visual role. The family grammar should define a finite set of named categories with explicit defaults and permitted exceptions, for example passive label, panel, loading placeholder, editable control, binary control, selected trigger, and scroll chrome. These names are working inventory labels, not pre-approved final entity names; the implementation must derive and validate the final category set against the current P entities and visual evidence.

Required governance boundary:

- exactly one applicable spec/knowledge or decision slice owns the family-level category grammar;
- component P entities reference or refine that owner and remain authoritative for their exact component criteria;
- every exception is finite, named, justified, and executable rather than an ad hoc source comment;
- the EN/ZH Design Contract becomes a traceable projection and must stop presenting an unqualified universal table;
- implementation normalization occurs only where several components are classified under the same invariant and currently drift from it;
- visual evidence covers every admitted category and exception in Light and Dark;
- generated tokens, presets, and CLI closure remain consistent when any token changes.

Do not create a second prose source of truth or infer that every current implementation difference deserves permanent exception status. First classify the existing Badge, Card, Skeleton, Textarea, Scroll Area, Toggle, Switch, and Tabs behavior; then either map each value to an approved category/exception or normalize it to that category default.

Design decision status: **typed grammar approved; category inventory, normative owner, projections, and executable evidence remain implementation work**.
